member.summary:
Reads and writes the bounded binary envelope for persistent bytecode.
Successful parsing verifies integrity but never grants compiler-output trust;
the returned artifact still requires the state's provenance validator.

Represents either an owned script closure or a managed callback capability.
Script closures and retained copies must be disposed before their root VM;
callback-borrowed closures are valid only for their active callback frame.

Compiles every source through the supplied bounded shared service. The
bundle is published only after every output and aggregate quota passes;
failures never expose a partially installable resolver.

Represents one managed Luau value. Primitive values are self-contained;
reference values borrow the lifetime of their contained wrapper and do not
retain it when this struct is copied or converted.
